    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0399" n="311" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg311"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860h.00/34: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-24T19:00:00+00:00"
                            >November 24, 1918—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 24—5:36 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>163. Referring to 106 [<hi rendition="#italic">120?</hi>]<anchor n="19a"
                        xml:id="d230-f1"/> and 145.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d230-f2"/> I have received
                    the following reply from the French Foreign Office: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“I have the honor to inform you that the French Government is favorable
                            to the presence, in regions of the former Austrian Hungarian Monarchy
                            where the populations are partly Italian and partly Jugo-Slav, of troops
                            belonging to the Allied countries who would not find themselves drawn
                            into conflicts of nationality. The French Government can, therefore,
                            only regard with pleasure the despatch of American troops to the
                            territories where they will find French detachments beside them.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
